WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:56.430
Tsunami! A tsunami is coming!

3
00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.600
[SANJI]
What is it now?

4
00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:00.360
[ZORO]
What's the matter, Luffy?

5
00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.730
Maybe it wasn't really such a good idea.

6
00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:04.030
[CHOPPER]
What wasn't a good idea?

7
00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:06.430
I warned him, but he didn't listen.

8
00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:08.600
He said he was so thirsty he couldn't stand it anymore,

9
00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:10.980
so he chomped down on some of
that cactus growing back there

10
00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:12.690
to suck out the moisture.

11
00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:13.890
[ZORO]
Cactus?

12
00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:16.180
Yep, right there.

13
00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:17.160
Those round things.

14
00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:18.650
[LUFFY]
A tsunami!

15
00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:21.160
Ah! You gotta be kidding!

16
00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.730
Those are mezcal cacti;

17
00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:24.640
they're used to make
hallucinogenic drugs!

18
00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:25.130
What?

19
00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:26.800
[LUFFY screaming]

20
00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:30.300
Look out! We're gonna drown!

21
00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:33.270
Right! Bring it on
if you got the guts!

22
00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:34.620
I'll beat you all up!

23
00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:38.490
[LUFFY yelling]

24
00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.260
Oh, crap.

25
00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:41.360
Gum-Gum...

26
00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:43.030
[USOPP, CHOPPER screaming]

27
00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.160
Heh. Knock-out!

28
00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.200
[SANJI]
Way to go, Chopper.

29
00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:54.950
<b>Yuba, the Town of Rebels</b>

30
00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:51.750
[CROCODILE]
The operation will
begin at the stroke of noon

31
00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:53.320
two days from now.

32
00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:55.390
Have you completed the arrangements?

33
00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:58.090
[MISS ALL SUNDAY]
Yes. Everything's in place.

34
00:02:58.090 --> 00:02:59.830
We have a hundred
and fifty Billions

35
00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:02.800
who are standing by in Nanohana.

36
00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:05.470
I've also called
Mister Two back here.

37
00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:07.800
It appears that he failed
utterly in his assignment

38
00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.480
to capture and
kill Mister Three.

39
00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.450
The officer agents have been instructed

40
00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.490
to gather tonight, at eight o'clock.

41
00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:17.420
They're meeting
at the Spiders Café.

42
00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:22.720
<b>The Spiders Cafe,
Baroque Works Headquarters
Kingdom of Alabasta</b>

43
00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:23.360
[CROCODILE]
Yes. Very good.

44
00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:25.460
[MISS ALL SUNDAY]
It's already past five o'clock.

45
00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:27.040
I would imagine that the officer agents

46
00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:29.980
will begin gathering at
the café any minute now.

47
00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:31.400
[music playing]

48
00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:49.620
[MISS MERRY CHRISTMAS]
Well, well! Merry Christmas!

49
00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:51.720
Merry Christmas!
That was an exhausting trip!

50
00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:54.000
My back is really killing me here!

51
00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:58.380
<b>Miss Merry Christmas
Officer Agent, Baroque Works</b>

52
00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:56.590
This is your fault, Mister Four!
You're so slow!

53
00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.960
If we had gotten here quicker,
my back wouldn't hurt right now!

54
00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:03.350
<b>Mr. 4
Officer Agent, Baroque Works</b>

55
00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:03.850
[MISTER FOUR]
Oh... I'm... sorry...

56
00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:06.630
Yes, yes, yes, yes! How's
business these days, Paula?

57
00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:08.540
The place sure is empty today!
It's an empty place.

58
00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:11.110
Place. Empty.
Place empty. Plempty!

59
00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.600
Well, it is certainly
good to see you again.

60
00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.740
Miss Merry Christmas
and you, Mister Four.

61
00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:26.080
<b>Paula, Proprietor, Spiders Cafe</b>

62
00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:19.810
You will have the shop all to yourselves for a while.

63
00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:21.580
I can go ahead and
brew some tea for you

64
00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:23.050
if you don't mind waiting a few minutes

65
00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:26.250
for it to steep. Is it chamomile
as usual, Mister Four?

66
00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:27.810
No! I don't wanna
wait for tea!

67
00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:29.150
I want something I can drink right now!

68
00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:31.290
Something fast! Right away!
Right away! No waiting!

69
00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:32.820
Right now, okay, got it?

70
00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:34.590
You seem to be in good spirits.

71
00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:36.110
Is work going well for you right now?

72
00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:38.080
In my line of work,
if you don't do well, you die.

73
00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.180
So obviously, it's going well.
You stupid woman.

74
00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.180
Stupid woman. Stuman! Stuman!

75
00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:45.180
[PAULA]
Of course, how forgetful of me.

76
00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:46.050
I'm sorry.

77
00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:47.220
[MISTER TWO]
Un, deux.

78
00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:48.120
[GROUP]
– Ora!
– Ora!

79
00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.690
[MISTER TWO]
Un, deux.

80
00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.220
What is that noise?

81
00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:53.010
What kind of crazy
singers are you using

82
00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:55.320
in this place these
days, anyhow?

83
00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:56.350
Singers?

84
00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:59.050
No, I have a classical sonata playing right now.

85
00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:02.360
There are no words.
There shouldn't be any singing.

86
00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:03.660
[MISTER TWO]
Un, deux.

87
00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:04.990
[GROUP]
– Ora!
– Ora!

88
00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:06.090
[PAULA]
Strange.

89
00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:07.140
[MISTER TWO]
Un, deux.

90
00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:07.500
[GROUP]
– Krah!
– Krah!

91
00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:08.340
[MISTER TWO]
Head in the clouds,
and feet on the ground

92
00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:10.890
and un, deux!

93
00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:11.750
[GROUP]
– Krah!
– Krah!

94
00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.190
[MISTER TWO]
Fly like a fish in a stream.

95
00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:14.660
Un, deux.

96
00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:15.830
[GROUP]
– Ora!
– Ora!

97
00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:19.330
Spin! Just remember!

98
00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:20.530
Spin!

99
00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:22.600
Spin!

100
00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:25.770
Pretty shoes!

101
00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.500
And mascara!

102
00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:31.880
Pretty shoes and mascara!

103
00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:38.090
[GROUP]
– I'm such a lovely dancing boy!
– I'm such a lovely dancing boy!

104
00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:41.850
Now! We say!

105
00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:42.950
Switch foot!

106
00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:43.920
[GROUP]
– Switch foot!
– Switch foot!

107
00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:44.930
[MISTER TWO]
And up!

108
00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:46.060
[GROUP]
– And up!
– And up!

109
00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:49.700
[MISTER TWO]
And now! Leap away!

110
00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:51.670
Let's hear you boys sing it!

111
00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:52.540
Mascara!

112
00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:53.340
[MAN B]
And shoes!

113
00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:54.200
[MAN C]
And a...

114
00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:55.840
[SUBORDINATE]
...tu-tu!

115
00:05:55.840 --> 00:06:00.850
[GROUP]
– Oh! Dance away!
– Oh! Dance away!

116
00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:58.130
Dance...

117
00:05:58.220 --> 00:05:59.020
Away!

118
00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:06.620
[MISTER TWO]
Hello to all!

119
00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:09.090
And how are deux today?

120
00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:10.120
Huh?

121
00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:12.120
[PAULA]
You're a freak.

122
00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:14.420
[MISTER TWO]
I am not a freak, Paula!

123
00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:17.460
I am merely a talented
dancer practicing my craft.

124
00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:19.360
I will take one sparkling water, please.

125
00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:20.360
[PAULA]
Don't have any.

126
00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:22.250
Don't have any?
Gimme a break!

127
00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:24.610
That's what all the high-class
ballerinas drink!

128
00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.400
[whines]

129
00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:27.660
[MISTER TWO]
Oh, you're still here?

130
00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:29.080
You guys can leave now.

131
00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.110
[GROUP]
– Right!
– Right!

132
00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:31.340
[MISTER TWO]
And don't forget to
practice those new

133
00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:33.480
dance moves like
we talked about.

134
00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:36.680
[GROUP]
– Right! Un, deux, un, deux.
– Right! Un, deux, un, deux.

135
00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:36.400
UN...

136
00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:35.620
De...

137
00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:37.670
How nice.

138
00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:39.610
The fatty and the
old hag are here with us.

139
00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:41.440
Why don't you just shut your fat mouth,

140
00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:43.350
you weirdo ballet-dancing,
swan-wearing

141
00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:44.290
freak of nature!

142
00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:46.500
Well! Nice to see you!

143
00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:47.400
Did you hear?

144
00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:49.040
It seems like even
Mister One's team

145
00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:50.980
is being mobilized
for this assignment.

146
00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.350
I've never actually had the pleasure

147
00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:55.020
of meeting him and his partner.

148
00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:56.520
I'm really very excited!

149
00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:59.520
[laughing]

150
00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:04.880
There's a little something I wanted you to have.

151
00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:05.920
Here.

152
00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:12.020
Do yourself a favor
and hang onto that.

153
00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:14.230
But it's just a scrap of paper.

154
00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:16.360
[ACE]
That paper will
reunite us some day.

155
00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:20.910
I'd tuck it away somewhere.
For safe keeping.

156
00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.580
What ya don't want it?

157
00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:24.080
No, I do.

158
00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:27.780
It's perfectly natural for a guy to worry...

159
00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:30.720
...about his
bungling kid brother.

160
00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:34.120
He might be a bit much
for all of you to handle...

161
00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:37.390
...but take good
care of him for me.

162
00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:40.330
Wait. You're leaving already?

163
00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:47.600
Luffy, when next we meet,
we'll both be top pirates.

164
00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:48.900
[LUFFY chuckles]

165
00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:11.770
[USOPP]
Hey, Luffy?

166
00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:12.800
[LUFFY]
Huh?

167
00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.570
[USOPP]
What was that thing
your brother gave you?

168
00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:16.170
[LUFFY]
I don't really know.

169
00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:18.680
Just looks like a scrap of paper.

170
00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:19.780
It's just paper?

171
00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:20.910
[SANJI]
Lemme see it.

172
00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:25.070
Well, it looks like it really
is just a piece of paper.

173
00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:27.020
There's nothing written on it or anything.

174
00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:31.670
Is that all? Really?

175
00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:33.610
[LUFFY]
I'm not really sure
why Ace gave it to me,

176
00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:35.230
but it's important. Ah...!

177
00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:37.630
[LUFFY]
Wahh...!

178
00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:39.800
Don't eat that!

179
00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:42.020
Dumb camel.

180
00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:43.690
Hey, Luffy. Give me your hat.

181
00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:44.690
Huh? Why?

182
00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:46.300
[NAMI]
If it's really
that important to you,

183
00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:48.540
I can sew it to the underside of your hat ribbon.

184
00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:50.640
[LUFFY]
Good idea!
Sew it on real good!

185
00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:51.660
[NAMI]
Yeah, yeah.

186
00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:55.000
[NAMI]
There, it's all done.

187
00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:57.740
Here you go.

188
00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.670
Now I don't have to worry about losing it.

189
00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:00.660
Thanks!

190
00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:02.210
If there isn't even
anything written on it,

191
00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:04.240
what's the point of
hanging onto the thing?

192
00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:06.340
Ace said it's important
and I should hang onto it.

193
00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:08.850
So I'm hanging on to it.
That's all.

194
00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:10.830
So, you're pretty much
just basing your decision

195
00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:11.700
on nothing.

196
00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:13.700
No, my instincts.
They're right a lot.

197
00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:15.840
[GROUP chattering]

198
00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:18.040
[USOPP]
Will someone please carry me?

199
00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:19.610
[MISTER TWO sighs]

200
00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:24.410
Moment by moment, the night grows later.

201
00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:26.780
We are nearing eight o'clock, the appointed time.

202
00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:38.820
[MISTER TWO]
Oh! I'm so bored!

203
00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:43.660
Time to practice my spinning!

204
00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:45.660
Yes, I'm bored, so I'm going for a spin.

205
00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:46.800
Around and around I go.

206
00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:48.760
Quit it! Just looking
at you hurts!

207
00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:49.520
Ooh!

208
00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:50.950
What's your problem,
you old hag?

209
00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:52.280
Do you wanna fight?

210
00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:54.460
Do you really think you can handle me?

211
00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:56.690
Come, now, why don't
you two cut it out?

212
00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:57.990
Stop fighting.

213
00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:03.430
[GROUP yells]

214
00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:10.540
Hey, what happened to you?

215
00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:11.710
Why are you lying there on the ground

216
00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:14.340
instead of practicing like
you're supposed to be doing?

217
00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.040
[SUBORDINATE]
We were! Until him!

218
00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:18.400
[MISTER ONE]
Oh.

219
00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:21.430
So these men are
acquaintances of yours?

220
00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:23.900
[MISTER ONE]
You see, I found
them acting suspicious

221
00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:35.490
<b>Mr. 1
Officer Agent, Baroque Works</b>

222
00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:26.900
out in the desert.

223
00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:29.710
Don't worry.
I doubt they'll die.

224
00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:32.980
You seem unnecessarily concerned about them.

225
00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:35.880
Fostering friendships will only make you weaker.

226
00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:38.480
Those men are mine!
They don't belong to you!

227
00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:40.020
You'd better stop, Mister Two!

228
00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:45.160
[MISTER TWO]
Un. Deux. Krah!

229
00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:48.900
[MISTER TWO]
Un. Deux. Krah!

230
00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:53.110
[laughing]

231
00:10:53.180 --> 00:10:55.950
Ball Change! Un. Deux!

232
00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:05.970
What the hell?

233
00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:07.900
He flew straight
through the wall!

234
00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:10.200
He barely seemed to notice it was happening!

235
00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:14.640
[MISTER ONE]
Do you want to die that badly?

236
00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:16.720
[MISS DOUBLEFINGER]
Hold it.

237
00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:18.590
That's enough playing
around, Mister One.

238
00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:19.620
I'm not done.

239
00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:21.810
Move, Miss Doublefinger.

240
00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:24.060
I still haven't killed him yet.

241
00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:25.930
[MR. 2]
Stop it! Come on!
Just get off of me, fatty!

242
00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:27.560
Oh! You're killing me...

243
00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:28.430
[MISS DOUBLEFINGER]
Mr. 2.

244
00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:30.680
It's time for you to
calm down as well.

245
00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:31.750
It's eight o'clock.

246
00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:36.160
All the agents that should be here are here.

247
00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:38.610
What's more, a letter
containing the orders

248
00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:41.480
has arrived at the
Spiders Café. So...

249
00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:45.120
We're instructed to head to Rainbase,

250
00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:47.580
the city of dreams.

251
00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:49.690
In that city, we'll meet someone.

252
00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:52.860
A man we know, but whose face we have never seen.

253
00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:55.260
[GROUP gasps]

254
00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:00.830
We're heading to meet the boss.

255
00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:08.910
[MISS ALL SUNDAY]
The officer agents should all be

256
00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:11.280
on their way here
to Rainbase as we speak.

257
00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:18.640
<b>Bunchi
Special All-Terrain Transport Turtle
Baroque Works</b>

258
00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:16.150
I sent Bunchi to get them.

259
00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:18.960
I expect them to arrive sometime later tonight.

260
00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:24.630
[MISTER TWO]
To think that
you've actually been

261
00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:26.630
Miss Doublefinger
this entire time.

262
00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:28.570
That's very interesting.

263
00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:34.230
<b>Miss Doublefinger
Officer Agent, Baroque Works</b>

264
00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:32.120
Who knows, perhaps
I would have told you.

265
00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:35.040
But none of you ever
asked me about it.

266
00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:37.370
[CROCODILE]
The Billions that we
lost in Nanohana...

267
00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:40.150
have you been able to find replacements?

268
00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:41.350
[MISS ALL SUNDAY]
I've made the assignments

269
00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:43.340
for the replacements.

270
00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:46.010
As far as contacting
the new Billions,

271
00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:48.940
I've dispatched the Lizard Runners to see to that.

272
00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:51.250
<b>Frilled Runners
Urgent Delivery Force
Baroque Works</b>

273
00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:57.350
Good to hear.

274
00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:59.030
Things are almost ready.

275
00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:06.670
[VIVI]
Look up ahead! I see a light.

276
00:13:06.670 --> 00:13:08.680
[LUFFY]
Does that mean
we made it to Yuba?

277
00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:11.540
I can't see with all this sand blowing everywhere.

278
00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:14.080
[VIVI]
Something here
doesn't feel right.

279
00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:17.990
There's something wrong
down there. I can tell.

280
00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:25.990
Oh, no!

281
00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:32.300
The entire city is being
struck by a sandstorm!

282
00:13:46.390 --> 00:13:47.390
Can't be.

283
00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:56.650
<b>Yuba Oasis
Kingdom of Alabasta</b>

284
00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:52.700
[ZORO]
It doesn't look good.

285
00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:54.200
This place doesn't look much different

286
00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:56.370
from that Erumalu
town from before.

287
00:13:58.200 --> 00:13:59.700
Water!

288
00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:01.540
Vivi, I thought this city
was supposed to be

289
00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:02.970
some sort of oasis.

290
00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:06.440
It looks like the
oasis has disappeared!

291
00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:08.540
It's been swallowed up
by all the sand!

292
00:14:08.770 --> 00:14:09.810
[shovel strikes]

293
00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:16.970
[TOTO]
I'm assuming
that you're travelers.

294
00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:20.470
You must be exhausted from
all the time spent in that heat.

295
00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:24.880
Sorry, but this town
is a bit dried up, too.

296
00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:28.410
It doesn't have much relief to offer.

297
00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:31.250
But still, you're free to rest here for a while.

298
00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:41.530
<b>Toto
A Man from Yuba</b>

299
00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:36.280
[TOTO]
We may not have much water,

300
00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:38.750
but there are plenty of inns here in the town.

301
00:14:38.870 --> 00:14:40.800
It's what we've prided
ourselves so much on,

302
00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:42.340
after all.

303
00:14:42.410 --> 00:14:44.480
[VIVI]
Thank you, but we came
here because we thought

304
00:14:44.510 --> 00:14:47.510
the rebel army was in this town.

305
00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:49.910
[TOTO]
What business do you
have with the rebel army?

306
00:14:49.940 --> 00:14:51.410
Curse all of you!

307
00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:52.980
If you're here to join the rebel army,

308
00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:55.290
you can just go back where you came from!

309
00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:01.770
[TOTO]
If you're looking for
those fools, look elsewhere.

310
00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:04.450
They're no longer in this town.

311
00:15:04.450 --> 00:15:06.320
Wait, they're gone?!

312
00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:08.710
They left?

313
00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:10.550
[TOTO]
I'm sure you noticed

314
00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:13.340
the town was just
hit by a sandstorm.

315
00:15:13.340 --> 00:15:15.440
But that one certainly wasn't the first.

316
00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:17.720
After three years of no rain,

317
00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:20.520
the land has become increasingly dry.

318
00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:23.830
Sandstorms became a regular occurrence here.

319
00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:25.890
Little by little,
the oasis that we knew

320
00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:27.700
was swallowed up.

321
00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:30.370
Until the town became what you see now.

322
00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:32.710
A dying wasteland.

323
00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:35.380
With the flow of supplies to the town ended,

324
00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:38.420
the rebel army couldn't maintain
their drawn-out struggle.

325
00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:40.380
So they packed up.

326
00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:41.550
They've moved on.

327
00:15:41.630 --> 00:15:44.400
The rebel base is now located in Katorea.

328
00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:47.660
[VIVI]
Katorea?

329
00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:48.830
Um, where's that?

330
00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:51.000
Is Katorea close to here, Vivi?

331
00:15:51.060 --> 00:15:53.760
It's near Nanohana.
Back the way we came from.

332
00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:55.100
[ZORO]
Well, great.

333
00:15:55.170 --> 00:15:58.540
Coming all this way was just a waste of time.

334
00:15:58.570 --> 00:16:01.070
[TOTO]
Vivi. Wait, your name's...

335
00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:04.010
Hold on! She's definitely
not a princess!

336
00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:05.410
Nice one, Luffy!

337
00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:09.900
[TOTO]
Princess Vivi?
Is that really you?

338
00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:13.760
You're alive!
I can't believe it!

339
00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:15.670
Thank goodness!

340
00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:19.570
It's me, Vivi.
Don't you recognize me?

341
00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:21.630
I look different.

342
00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:24.060
I lost some weight, I suppose.

343
00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:26.600
Toto! Is it really you?

344
00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:30.090
That's right.

345
00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:36.470
[VIVI]
It can't be.

346
00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:43.610
[TOTO]
So long, my princess.

347
00:16:43.610 --> 00:16:45.950
We won't see you for a while.

348
00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:47.620
As soon as Yuba's
up and running,

349
00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:49.130
stop by, Princess.

350
00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:51.040
Yes, of course I will, Toto.

351
00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:56.440
[TOTO]
Yuba is going to do
a great deal for this dry,

352
00:16:56.480 --> 00:16:57.980
desert country of ours.

353
00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:01.980
[TOTO]
I know it.

354
00:17:11.650 --> 00:17:13.920
Toto? That's this guy?

355
00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:16.960
Whatever it's worth, Vivi dear,

356
00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:19.160
I have faith in you and the king.

357
00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:23.500
He's a good man.

358
00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:26.870
A true king who would
never betray his country.

359
00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:28.040
I know it.

360
00:17:28.050 --> 00:17:34.950
[TOTO crying]

361
00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:51.910
[TOTO crying]

362
00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:01.150
This rebellion is ridiculous!

363
00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:04.480
A bunch of faithless fools.

364
00:18:05.820 --> 00:18:06.990
See ya, Vivi!

365
00:18:06.990 --> 00:18:09.730
I hope ya grow up to become
a great princess someday!

366
00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:10.390
'Kay!

367
00:18:10.390 --> 00:18:12.330
[laughing]

368
00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:26.250
<b>Kingdom of Alabasta
11 Years Ago</b>

369
00:18:45.210 --> 00:18:47.450
[KOZA]
We-We need help!

370
00:18:47.150 --> 00:18:50.440
<b>Koza
A Boy from Town</b>

371
00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:48.950
Our village has dried up!

372
00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:51.290
How can you sit there
and do nothing?!

373
00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:54.560
Weather is beyond my control as king.

374
00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:56.380
I cannot command nature.

375
00:18:56.380 --> 00:19:00.180
It is beyond any man's power.
There's nothing I can do.

376
00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:03.020
[KOZA]
My dad always told me
the king's power is limitless...

377
00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:04.900
he can do anything he wishes!

378
00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:07.260
My abilities exist only in the realm of men.

379
00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:08.420
I'm not some kind of god...

380
00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:09.390
[MESSENGER]
Your Highness!

381
00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:11.990
This boy's father's
come to the palace!

382
00:19:11.990 --> 00:19:14.500
[TOTO]
My deepest apologizes,
Your Majesty! It's my fault.

383
00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:18.350
<b>Toto, the Boy's Father
(The Man from Yuba)</b>

384
00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:16.400
Forgive my stupid son, Sire!

385
00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:19.130
Place the punishment
for his actions on me!

386
00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:21.550
I'll accept any penalties!
It's my fault!

387
00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:24.350
Please, I beg of you!

388
00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:25.520
What were you thinking?

389
00:19:25.550 --> 00:19:26.890
How dare you!

390
00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:30.890
You're stupid, insolent,
thoughtless...

391
00:19:30.910 --> 00:19:31.610
An idiot!

392
00:19:31.610 --> 00:19:34.880
Your name is Toto, is it not?

393
00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:35.970
Yes!

394
00:19:36.010 --> 00:19:38.140
[COBRA]
I will officially grant
temporary sanctuary

395
00:19:38.180 --> 00:19:40.480
to any villagers who are
suffering due to the crisis

396
00:19:40.510 --> 00:19:41.800
caused by this drought.

397
00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:43.430
You're welcome to live here.

398
00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:47.170
Alubarna is a fine place for you to plan for your future.

399
00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:49.910
[TOTO]
Oh, we appreciate
your benevolence, King!

400
00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:53.840
Thank you, Sire!
Thank you, Sire!

401
00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:56.010
Whatever! I don't wanna
live in this stupid capital!

402
00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:58.020
Is that the best you
can do for us?!

403
00:19:58.080 --> 00:20:00.980
[TOTO]
Wait, Koza! Get back here!

404
00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:03.990
Mr. Toto.

405
00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:06.350
[TOTO]
Yes, Sire! As you say!

406
00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:07.180
[COBRA]
Your son's comments

407
00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:10.000
represent the people's
frustrations.

408
00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:11.200
He's a good boy.

409
00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:14.070
He cares for those who suffer.

410
00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:17.340
That is why he is acting in such a way.

411
00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:23.270
Hey there, crybaby.

412
00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:28.170
What did you say to me, midget?

413
00:20:28.170 --> 00:20:28.750
Midget?

414
00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:30.220
[IGARAM]
King Cobra.

415
00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:31.690
Igaram, what's the matter?

416
00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:32.820
[IGARAM]
With all due respect,

417
00:20:32.820 --> 00:20:35.490
it's unrealistic to think
we can support them all,

418
00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:37.990
not without exhausting
our funds, Sire.

419
00:20:38.020 --> 00:20:39.160
[COBRA]
You fool!

420
00:20:39.190 --> 00:20:41.520
We will bear the burden of
this crisis with our people.

421
00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:43.520
Their pleas will not be ignored.

422
00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:47.050
I understand. As you wish.

423
00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:48.120
[MESSENGER]
It's terrible.

424
00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:50.690
Your Majesty!
It's Princess Vivi!

425
00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:55.540
I fought with that boy,
and got beaten.

426
00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:57.780
– Vivi!
– Ah! Princess Vivi!

427
00:20:57.810 --> 00:20:59.650
How dare a commoner lay even a finger

428
00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:00.980
on a member of this
esteemed house.

429
00:21:01.050 --> 00:21:01.880
That boy's dead!

430
00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:04.720
No! Wait! Igaram,
you must calm down!

431
00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:07.720
[TOTO]
Your Majesty,
my deepest apologies!

432
00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:10.490
Please, Sire, kill me instead!

433
00:21:10.560 --> 00:21:12.930
[COBRA]
You're both idiots!

434
00:21:17.570 --> 00:21:20.940
You fools. It was a
children's quarrel!

435
00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:27.810
<b>Capital City, Alubarna</b>

436
00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:29.980
<b>City Outskirts</b>

437
00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:32.060
Fruit on sale!

438
00:21:32.090 --> 00:21:33.260
[RUNNING BOY]
Fight! Fight!

439
00:21:33.290 --> 00:21:36.230
[KIDS shouting]

440
00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:39.330
Teach that snotty princess
a lesson! Take her down!

441
00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:41.400
[KID C, KID D]
– Go, Vivi! Beat him.
– Go, Vivi! Beat him.

442
00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:42.430
Shut up, traitors!

443
00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:45.550
Don't ya know we're supposed
to cheer for Koza?!

444
00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:53.260
I become your leader when I
beat you, that's the deal!

445
00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:55.660
[KOZA]
I'd never lose
a fight to you, midget!

446
00:21:55.720 --> 00:21:59.630
I've never lost a fight.
Especially to a dumb girl!

447
00:22:00.660 --> 00:22:01.690
Is that right?

448
00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:04.750
[KIDS yelling]

449
00:22:04.750 --> 00:22:07.420
[KID A, KID B]
– You can do it, Koza! Fight!
– You can do it, Koza! Fight!

450
00:22:07.420 --> 00:22:09.660
[KID C, KID D]
– Go, Princess, go!
– Go, Princess, go!

451
00:22:17.810 --> 00:22:19.670
All right, you guys, listen up!

452
00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:22.440
As of today, Princess
Vivi will be vice-leader

453
00:22:22.470 --> 00:22:23.800
of the Sand-Sand Clan!

454
00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:25.610
Does anyone have a
problem with that?!

455
00:22:25.640 --> 00:22:29.280
[KIDS]
– No!
– No!

456
00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:31.680
[COBRA]
Look, Igaram.

457
00:22:31.720 --> 00:22:34.490
Vivi has made some new friends.

458
00:22:34.490 --> 00:22:35.390
Yes, Sire.

459
00:22:35.390 --> 00:22:37.340
That is the most important thing to have

460
00:22:37.340 --> 00:22:40.110
if she's to rule Alabasta in my stead.

461
00:22:40.180 --> 00:22:42.680
The people must follow her.

462
00:22:48.190 --> 00:22:49.360
[chuckles]

463
00:22:50.860 --> 00:22:52.770
[VIVI]
Toto! Ma'am!

464
00:22:52.770 --> 00:22:54.830
Good morning! Where's Leader?

465
00:22:54.830 --> 00:22:56.530
Oh, good morning!

466
00:22:56.570 --> 00:22:59.010
If you're looking for Koza, he already left.

467
00:22:59.110 --> 00:23:01.180
I assume he's at the usual spot.

468
00:23:01.300 --> 00:23:03.310
See ya later!

469
00:23:03.310 --> 00:23:06.310
Hey, Vivi! You coming for lunch?

470
00:23:06.350 --> 00:23:09.550
Yes, please!
Thank you very much!

471
00:23:09.590 --> 00:23:11.860
What a strange country we live in.

472
00:23:11.890 --> 00:23:14.730
The princess mingling
with commoners like us,

473
00:23:14.760 --> 00:23:16.470
who would've ever thought?

474
00:23:16.470 --> 00:23:19.340
A sign of peaceful times.

475
00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:21.310
[TOTO]
And will you be joining us?

476
00:23:21.340 --> 00:23:23.060
No, no, that's quite all right.

477
00:23:23.060 --> 00:23:25.630
I packed a lunch today. Bye!

478
00:23:33.270 --> 00:23:34.540
[COBRA]
Shh!

479
00:23:34.570 --> 00:23:38.040
Your Majesty! What are
you doing here?!

480
00:23:38.080 --> 00:23:41.380
Cobra! My lord! Ugh...

481
00:23:41.380 --> 00:23:43.620
I asked you not to
follow me again.

482
00:23:43.770 --> 00:23:45.270
Yeah, it's just,

483
00:23:45.330 --> 00:23:48.900
I wanted to make sure my
precious daughter's okay.

484
00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:50.210
[growls]

485
00:23:50.280 --> 00:23:51.180
Go home, Sire!

486
00:23:51.210 --> 00:23:53.780
I can't babysit you and Princess Vivi, too!

487
00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:55.180
What?!

488
00:23:55.220 --> 00:23:56.190
Go home!

489
00:23:56.190 --> 00:23:57.650
You heard me!

490
00:24:07.560 --> 00:24:09.800
What a sweet story, Vivi.

491
00:24:09.800 --> 00:24:11.700
[USOPP]
Luffy, stop it!

492
00:24:11.700 --> 00:24:13.460
Hello, Princess!

493
00:24:13.530 --> 00:24:17.100
You lost, little girl?
We'll help you out.

494
00:24:19.640 --> 00:24:21.370
Protect her, Sand-Sand Clan!

495
00:24:21.400 --> 00:24:23.270
[KIDS yelling]

496
00:24:23.310 --> 00:24:25.240
[BAD GUY A]
What the hell's
wrong with these kids?!

497
00:24:25.360 --> 00:24:27.800
They won't give up!

498
00:24:27.940 --> 00:24:29.610
Leader! Guys!

499
00:24:29.640 --> 00:24:30.680
Vivi! Get going!

500
00:24:30.740 --> 00:24:33.010
We're trying to hold these
guys off for you! Go!

501
00:24:33.080 --> 00:24:34.950
Vivi, get outta here right now!

502
00:24:34.980 --> 00:24:36.520
Yeah, you gotta run, now!

503
00:24:36.590 --> 00:24:38.820
I can't... Leader!

504
00:24:38.850 --> 00:24:40.710
[BAD GUY A laughs]

505
00:24:40.710 --> 00:24:41.810
We're not here to kill you.

506
00:24:41.870 --> 00:24:45.100
We just wanna kidnap you for
a ransom from your father,

507
00:24:45.140 --> 00:24:47.210
but these other kids...

508
00:24:48.240 --> 00:24:50.040
Damn!

509
00:24:50.080 --> 00:24:53.710
Okay. Now just come with
us quietly, Princess Vivi.

510
00:24:55.320 --> 00:24:57.820
[BOTH laugh]

511
00:24:57.880 --> 00:24:59.550
[KOZA]
Step back!

512
00:24:59.550 --> 00:25:01.820
Protect her to the death,
Sand-Sand Clan!
